```c
-    /* Power gate DSCs */
-    if (!is_optimized_init_done) {
-        for (i = 0; i < res_pool->res_cap->num_dsc; i++)
-            if (hws->funcs.dsc_pg_control != NULL)
-                hws->funcs.dsc_pg_control(hws, res_pool->dscs[i]->inst, false);
-    }
```
Reason:
Removing the redundant DSC power gating code from `dcn10_init_hw` ensures that the DSC power gating is only handled in `init_pipes()`, thus preventing duplicated actions and potential conflicts during hardware initialization across different versions. This change aligns the initialization process and maintains consistent power states.

